{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794931548,"nonce":"4cJAi86wMZyvJ6riCNBdctckINk=","message":"Implementation and validation have advanced locally in hxn-audio and the existing hxn-av library; no source commits, pushes, publication, or git-bug push have been made.\n\nhxn-av now reuses its xavi CPU media/PCM/equalizer/configuration/chunk/queue operations on wasm, with a bounded WebCodecs AAC-LC AudioDecoder behind the existing Haxe create/tryDecode/poll/read/finish/close API. Guest input is copied before acknowledgment; async callbacks own page results only; read copies PCM synchronously into caller-owned storage. Input/output item and byte credits, errors, EOF and late-callback close behavior are explicit. Encoding, browser MP4/file access/player and video decoding remain unavailable. Native codec workers remain unchanged. Ash uses its host-agent/build/serve workflow; unthreaded Emscripten starts no native codec threads. Source/installed init macros ship and copy browser assets. Browser CI/release jobs, skills and current design/convention docs are updated. Emscripten media packages reserve a 1 MiB stack; the full debug equalizer check exposed exhaustion of the default stack.\n\nThe installed hxn audio check --av decodes 48 AAC packets into 49,152 frames, transfers through a 257-frame ring to force suffix retries, and asserts the stream consumes exactly every transferred frame while overlapping sounds play. It passes on macOS/Ash and hxcpp; Ash wasm, unthreaded hxcpp and threaded hxcpp in Chrome; iOS 17.5 simulator/Ash and hxcpp; Android emulator/Ash and hxcpp. Browser integration checks were repeated serially. Native estimates are about 11 ms on macOS, 8 ms on the iOS simulator and 156–159 ms on the emulator; WebAudio reports about 37 ms. These are backend timestamp estimates, not acoustic loopback measurements. Pixel audibility is the separate user-confirmed hxcpp listening check already recorded: about 25.6 ms, unchanged media volume. The Pixel disconnected before decoded-stream physical testing, so emulator results do not cover that missing evidence. Simulators/devices are restored and temporary test APKs removed.\n\nThe new core has 10 functional tests plus 2 real-time/concurrency tests; DSP ownership adds one. All pass, including render allocation/free audits, dynamic bus changes, exact stream EOF position and repeated 64,000-frame concurrent transfers. Functional tests and the DSP control/render ownership test pass under Miri. DSP Miri uses the integer-address ABI and emits its expected provenance caveat; it is not strict-provenance proof. A two-instance wasm regression uploads 32 MiB PCM, grows shared memory, reuses one 64 MiB PCM allocation across voices and reads the preallocated output through the original shared view; it passes and is included in browser CI. Rust formatting, clippy with warnings denied and Haxe formatter pass. hxn-av's independent browser check passes PCM, equalizer, AAC backpressure, EOF and closed-handle assertions on all three runtimes; native Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp and CPPIA checks pass.\n\nhxn's cross-build linker-metadata defect is tracked in ab05ce629f82aeb2de812268ade5cae647945bd22e828675a4471a2c57dec0e8. Its local fix excludes host build-dependency libraries/search paths using Cargo's selected-target out_dir, with a regression containing host and target messages. Parent hxn workspace tests, clippy, CLI 39 tests, counter/generated bindings, every example, CLI packaging/plugin checks, C imports, web futures and all browser modes pass on the available macOS runtimes. Counter Ash JIT/interpreter use temporary executable adapters because that test script expects an executable path, not VM options. Parent hxcpp mobile examples pass on iOS simulator and Android emulator. Stock HashLink is unavailable on this Mac. Windows/Linux CI and a second-machine run have not run for these uncommitted changes; upstream CLI release ordering remains required for the new cross-packaging fix.\n\nKeep this issue and the browser-media prerequisite open pending CI, physical decoded-stream coverage and release/integration. Real headset unplug/interruption/audio-focus transitions, Safari/Firefox, Windows/Linux audio devices and acoustic loopback remain unverified. Apple native media objects also emit deployment-target warnings with the current SDK; the tested iOS 17.5 simulator passes, which does not establish support for older deployment targets. Do not turn these limits into a blanket platform pass.","files":null}]}